  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA, multi-profile, PCA, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc, and avgpool clearly outperforms transformer (0.591 vs 0.519). PCA outperformed scGPT in single-profile (0.485 vs 0.411), but we haven't tested scvi_n200 under the proven multi-profile + avgpool setting. Question: Does the learned scvi_n200 encoder capture complementary biological signal beyond PCA when combined with the best profile/aggregation combo? This isolates a single variable (RNA encoder) while holding profile=multiprofile and aggregation=avgpool constant, making it a clean comparison against config_002. Why this is the best use: With only 4 experiments remaining, confirming or ruling out a better RNA encoder before committing to multimodal fusion experiments is critical—if scvi_n200 improves the RNA backbone, subsequent multimodal runs should use it; if not, we confirm PCA as optimal and can dedicate remaining budget to testing whether adding image (config_018/019) provides any gain over the 0.591 baseline."
}

